{
  "id": "factor-theory",
  "term": "factor theory",
  "definition": "In this source, factor theory refers to conversion factor theory: the idea that people’s outcomes depend not just on available resources but on the conditions that affect how those resources can be turned into real opportunities and capabilities. Here, institutional features such as curriculum rules are treated as factors that shape whether career guidance becomes meaningful vocational capability.",
